n            return\n        if self._downloader:\n            format_sort = self._downloader.params.get('format_sort')\n        else:\n            format_sort = []\n        ...\n        formats.sort(key=lambda f: ...)\n```\n\nI'm fairly sure older versions are:\n\n```python\n    def _sort_formats(self, formats):\n        if not formats:\n            return\n        if self._downloader is not None:\n            preferences = self._downloader.params.get('format_sort', [])\n        else:\n            preferences = []\n```\n\nWhatever \u2014 get_info will tell.\n\n6. Instantiation: `LinuxAcademyIE()` \u2014 check `InfoExtractor.__init__` accepts no required args. Standard: `def __init__(self, downloader=None):`. \u2713.\n\n7. `ie_key()`: classmethod:\n\n```python\n    @classmethod\n    def ie_key(cls):\n        \"\"\"A string for getting the IE with get_info_extractor. Valid return values: get_info_extractor's key\"\"\"\n        return cls._IE_KEY if hasattr(cls, '_IE_KEY') else cls._IE_NAME\n```\n\nHmm, actually:\n\n```python\n    @classmethod\n    def ie_key(cls):\n        cls_val = getattr(cls, '_IE_KEY', None)\n        if cls_val:\n            return cls_val\n        return cls.ie_name()\n```\n\nsomething like that. LinuxAcademyIE likely has no _IE_KEY \u2192 returns ie_name() = 'LinuxAcademy' (from _IE_NAME = 'LinuxAcademy'). Assert equals `LinuxAcademyIE.ie_key()` \u2014 robust.\n\n8. Import path: `from youtube_dl.extractor.linuxacademy import LinuxAcademyIE`. The `youtube_dl.extractor` package `__init__` imports all extractors (gen-extractor modules list) \u2014 heavy but fine.\n\n9. State pollution: we create fresh IE per test; monkeypatch reverts instance attrs (monkeypatch.setattr on instance attr works and undoes). Global state: none modified. `json` etc fine.\n\n10. The `_VALID_URL` matching \u2014 pending get_info.\n\n11. One more: `mobj.group('chapter_id', 'lesson_id', 'course_id')` \u2014 for course URL, chapter_id/lesson_id may be None; item_id = course_id. For single URL, course_id None \u2192 item_id = 'chapter-lesson'.\n\n12. For the course test, `_download_webpage` receives (url, item_id) \u2014 assert downloaded['video_id'] == course_id.\n\n13. For single tests, assert downloaded['video_id'] == 'chapterid-lessonid'.\n\nNow \u2014 the URL formats. Let me now actually run get_info. I'll batch these calls:\n\n- LinuxAcademyIE\n- LinuxAcademyIE._VALID_URL\n- InfoExtractor._sort_formats\n- InfoExtractor._download_webpage\n- InfoExtractor._extract_m3u8_formats\n- InfoExtractor.__init__\n\nPossibly also:\n- urljoin (utils)\n- InfoExtractor._search_regex\n- InfoExtractor._parse_json\n- LinuxAcademyIE._real_extract\n\nLet me do a big batch \u2014 all independent.\n\nAfter that, compose the final test script.\n\nLet me pre-draft the test script with placeholders for URLs, then finalize after seeing _VALID_URL.\n\n```python\n# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n\"\"\"Tests for youtube_dl.extractor.linuxacademy.LinuxAcademyIE._real_extract.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import unicode_literals\n\nimport json\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom youtube_dl.extractor.linuxacademy import LinuxAcademyIE\nfrom youtube_dl.utils import parse_duration, unified_timestamp\n\n\nDEFAULT_FORMATS = [\n    {\n        'format_id': 'hls-720',\n        'url': 'https://cdn.example.com/hls/720.m3u8',\n        'ext': 'mp4',\n        'protocol': 'm3u8_native',\n        'height': 720,\n        'tbr': 2500,\n    },\n    {\n        'format_id': 'hls-360',\n        'url': 'https://cdn.example.com/hls/360.m3u8',\n        'ext': 'mp4',\n        'protocol': 'm3u8_native',\n        'height': 360,\n        'tbr': 900,\n    },\n]\n\n\nclass _FakeYDL(object):\n    \"\"\"Minimal stand-in for a YoutubeDL downloader (only .params is used).\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.params = {}\n\n\ndef _instrument_ie(monkeypatch, webpage, formats=None):\n    \"\"\"Build a LinuxAcademyIE with network-touching methods replaced.\"\"\"\n    ie = LinuxAcademyIE(_FakeYDL())\n\n    downloads = []\n    m3u8_calls = []\n    sort_calls = []\n\n    def fake_download_webpage(url_or_request, video_id, *args, **kwargs):\n        downloads.append({'url': url_or_request, 'video_id': video_id})\n        return webpage\n\n    def fake_extract_m3u8_formats(m3u8_url, video_id, ext=None,\n                                  entry_protocol='m3u8', **kwargs):\n        m3u8_calls.append({\n            'm3u8_url': m3u8_url,\n            'video_id': video_id,\n            'ext': ext,\n            'entry_protocol': entry_protocol,\n            'm3u8_id': kwargs.get('m3u8_id'),\n        })\n        return [dict(f) for f in (formats if formats is not None else DEFAULT_FORMATS)]\n\n    real_sort = LinuxAcademyIE._sort_formats\n\n    def spy_sort(fmts):\n        sort_calls.append(fmts)\n        real_sort(ie, fmts)\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_download_webpage', fake_download_webpage)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_extract_m3u8_formats', fake_extract_m3u8_formats)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_sort_formats', spy_sort)\n    return ie, downloads, m3u8_calls, sort_calls\n```\n\nWait: `LinuxAcademyIE(_FakeYDL())` \u2014 InfoExtractor.__init__(self, downloader=None) \u2192 ok.\n\nHmm, but if `_sort_formats` implementation differs (e.g., takes (self, formats, field_preference)), spy signature must adapt. Use *args:\n\n```python\n    def spy_sort(*args):\n        sort_calls.append(args[1])\n        real_sort(*args)\n```\n\nSafer.\n\nCourse webpage:\n\n```python\ndef _course_webpage():\n    module = {\n        'title': 'Linux Academy Course',\n        'md_desc': '',\n        'desc': '<b>Course HTML Description</b>',\n        'duration': '1:30:00',\n        'items': [\n            'not-a-dict',                                   # non-dict -> skipped\n            {},                                             # no type -> skipped\n            {                                               # section #1\n                'type': {'name': 'Section', 'slug': 'section'},\n                'course_name': 'Chapter One',\n                'course_module': 'module-1',\n            },\n            {                                               # quiz -> skipped\n                'type': {'name': 'Quiz'},\n            },\n            {                                               # lesson without url -> skipped\n                'type': {'name': 'lesson'},\n                'title': 'Orphan Lesson',\n            },\n            {                                               # full lesson\n                'type': {'name': 'lesson', 'slug': 'LESSON'},\n                'url': '/lesson/intro',\n                'title': 'Intro Lesson',\n                'md_desc': 'Intro markdown description',\n                'date': '2019-06-25T10:30:00Z',\n                'duration': '1:30:00',\n            },\n            {                                               # section #2\n                'type': {'name': 'SECTION'},\n                'course_name': 'Chapter Two',\n                'course_module': 'module-2',\n            },\n            {                                               # lesson w/ fallbacks\n                'type': {'slug': 'lesson'},\n                'url': 'https://linuxacademy.com/lesson/fallback',\n                'lesson_name': 'Fallback Lesson',\n                'description': '<i>Fallback description</i>',\n                'created_on': '2019-06-26 08:00:00',\n                'duration': '45:00',\n            },\n            {                                               # text-only description\n                'type': {'slug': 'lesson'},\n                'url': '/lesson/text-only',\n                'title': 'Text Only Lesson',\n                'text': '<b>Text description</b>',\n            },\n        ],\n    }\n    return '<html><head><script>window.module = %s;</script></head><body>x</body></html>' % (\n        json.dumps(module),)\n```\n\nCheck section #2: type name 'SECTION'.lower()='section' \u2192 in type_fields \u2192 section bra