doesn't match newline. So JSON must be on one line! Ensure json.dumps produces single-line (default separators produce no newlines). Good \u2014 keep compact.\n\nAlso `.+?` non-greedy up to `}` followed by `\\s*;` \u2014 nested braces inside JSON: non-greedy will stop at first `}` that is followed by optional whitespace and `;`. Our JSON ends with `}};`? The module object contains nested objects (items with dicts). The regex `({.+?})\\s*;` \u2014 it scans for `{`, then lazily expands until a `}` immediately followed by `;`. Nested closing braces are followed by `,` or `]` etc., not `;`, so expansion continues to the final `}` before `;`. But wait \u2014 lazy matching: it tries shortest match such that the remainder matches `\\s*;`. At each position of `}`, regex checks if next chars match `\\s*;`. Inside JSON, `}` followed by `,` fails; eventually last `}` followed by `;` succeeds. But what if a nested `}` is followed by whitespace then `;`? Only if JSON formatting puts `;` right after a nested close \u2014 not in our generated JSON. Good.\n\nSame for `player\\.playlist\\s*=\\s*(\\[.+?\\])\\s*;` \u2014 array must end with `];`. And `window\\.lesson\\s*=\\s*({.+?})\\s*;`.\n\nImportant: the lesson regexes are tried in order `(window\\.lesson..., player\\.lesson...)`; `_search_regex` iterates patterns. For the player.lesson test, ensure 'window.lesson' absent.\n\nTitle fallback regexes: `>Lecture\\s*:\\s*(?P<value>[^<]+)` \u2014 e.g., `<h1>Lecture : Foo</h1>` \u2014 wait, needs `>` before 'Lecture': `<h1>Lecture : Foo` \u2192 the char before 'Lecture' is '>' from `<h1>`. Match: `>Lecture\\s*:\\s*` then `[^<]+` captures 'Foo' (up to `<`). Value may include trailing spaces? `[^<]+` greedy \u2192 'Foo' if followed by '<'. If text is 'Lecture : Foo</h1>', captures 'Foo'. Good. Note `_search_regex` with group='value' returns that group. Trailing whitespace? 'Foo' clean.\n\nSecond alt: `lessonName\\s*=\\s*([\"\\'])(?P<value>(?:(?!\\1).)+)\\1` \u2014 e.g., `var lessonName = \